WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:01:00.000
Sofia Tremblay: Welcome everyone. Goal today is winter-readiness alignment before the next snowfall window.

00:01:00.000 --> 00:02:30.000
Amrita Patel: Store 214 completed 43 tire appointments Friday, average wait 24 minutes, and protected seven at-risk bookings.

00:02:30.000 --> 00:04:00.000
Jordan Singh: Completion is 92.5% this week. We moved 14 appointments and had 2 no-shows. Keep CAD 25 credits for >48h moves.

00:04:00.000 --> 00:05:30.000
David Nguyen: Store 118 saw queue spikes during weather alerts. We need a district-wide revised-window SMS template.

00:05:30.000 --> 00:07:00.000
Priya Raman: Store 327 found a 4-unit battery variance. We need daily cycle counts on top 25 winter SKUs.

00:07:00.000 --> 00:08:30.000
Sofia Tremblay: Decisions: keep 24h + 2h reminders, keep CAD 25 credit through Nov 30, and require daily top-25 SKU cycle counts.

00:08:30.000 --> 00:10:30.000
David Nguyen: Holding two weather-flex slots hurts conversion.
Jordan Singh: Without weather-flex slots we cancel safety-critical installs.
Amrita Patel: Release one slot by 11:00 if radar risk is low.
Sofia Tremblay: Trial one protected plus one conditional slot for two weeks.

00:10:30.000 --> 00:12:00.000
Sofia Tremblay: Action items assigned to Jordan, Amrita, Priya, and David with due dates Nov 10-12.

00:12:00.000 --> 00:13:30.000
Sofia Tremblay: Unresolved question: funding model for repeated expedited courier overages.

00:13:30.000 --> 00:14:30.000
Sofia Tremblay: Post daily updates in district Teams channel by 16:30 local.
